            <ArticleTitle>Transient phrenic nerve paralysis associated with status asthmaticus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>269-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Phrenic nerve paralysis is a condition typically occurring after invasive procedures in the chest and neck. Here we describe a case of transient unilateral diaphragmatic paralysis in a child with status asthmaticus complicated by complete right lung atelectasis. Common causes of this disorder and possible implications for our case are discussed.</AbstractText>
